  "notes": [
    "All Rust changes in this experiment are test-only; production behavior is unchanged.",
    "Initial candidate target discovery caused a dependency cycle. That failure is archived, and later binaries use typed producer metadata.",
    "Ranges binary supports the initial candidate modes and final lookup algorithms. The lookup matrix and actual-job lookup profiles use those algorithms.",
    "Typed profiles add Known/NotApplicable/Unknown eligibility and the independent EXISTS guard before stable setup.",
    "Setup binary adds automatic reprepare counters and connection-lifetime registration. Its input-version test fails because an adopted-binding owner is short-lived.",
    "Final binary retains that binding owner for the connection lifetime. All nine composition tests pass. Final profiles, edge jobs, positive job, and alternating timings use this binary.",
    "Full-corpus profile variants run separately; final alternating timings compare baseline against stable setup with typed candidates and nonempty frames.",
    "All builds and engine workloads use nice level 19. Other worktrees also built on the shared host; wall-time ratios are descriptive.",
    "Every profile JSON retains generated SQL and EXPLAIN decisions. Separate SQL/EQP extracts are provided for the setup and final series.",
    "The early range producer reduces VM instructions but loses CPU; its rejected timing results are archived.",
    "The SQL-only candidate rewrite happens after source projection planning. Deferred projection is an integration requirement, not a measured win in these spikes."
  ]
}
